menu "WiFi Dap wired DAP (C1: USB-NCM MVP)"

    choice BIRDIEBOT_WIRED_TRANSPORT
        prompt "DAP transport"
        default BIRDIEBOT_WIRED_TRANSPORT_NONE
        help
            C1 wired-DAP MVP: move the DAP transport from Wi-Fi to a wired USB
            link while keeping the existing USBIP/OpenOCD tool-chain.
            Design/effort/risks: docs/wired-dap-plan.md and docs/wired-dap-mvp.md.

            The DEFAULT is NONE: the production Wi-Fi-only behaviour is
            unchanged and the default `build/esp32s3` (and C3/ESP32) artifacts
            are not affected.

            The wired variant is a separate build:
                scripts/build-wired.sh
            which applies sdkconfig.wired.defaults and produces
            build/esp32s3-wired/. It is not part of the default release matrix.

        config BIRDIEBOT_WIRED_TRANSPORT_NONE
            bool "Wi-Fi only (default, production behaviour)"

        config BIRDIEBOT_WIRED_TRANSPORT_NCM
            bool "USB-NCM Ethernet + existing USBIP/OpenOCD (wired MVP)"
            depends on SOC_USB_OTG_SUPPORTED
            help
                TinyUSB CDC-NCM on the ESP32-S3 native USB-OTG port plus a
                minimal esp_netif/lwIP Ethernet driver:

                  device IP (static): 192.168.7.1/24
                  DAP proxy:          existing TCP 3240 (USBIP/elaphureLink/WS-DAP)
                  host setup:         USB NCM network adapter 192.168.7.2/24
                                      + `usbip attach_ude -r 192.168.7.1 -b 1-1`
                                      + unchanged OpenOCD command line.

                Building this option requires (scripts/build-wired.sh applies
                both automatically):
                  - CONFIG_TINYUSB_NET_MODE_NCM=y (esp_tinyusb component)
                  - CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_SECONDARY_NONE=y
                    (USB-OTG and USB-Serial/JTAG cannot be active at the same
                     time; the wired build keeps the console on UART0)

                Flashing/recovery for a wired build: BOOT+RESET into the ROM
                USB-Serial/JTAG download mode, UART0 download, or Web UI OTA
                (Wi-Fi is kept enabled; see docs/wired-dap-mvp.md §4).
    endchoice

endmenu
